# tools/gen/season/cion_module_labeling_witness.rish — CION, the widened labeling guard.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/gen/season/cion_module_labeling_witness.rish
#
# The CION sweep past the three living pins (which grad_seal already guards): module
# living surfaces — a module's README and its authored .rye doc-comments — carry no
# bare "lap N" capability identity. The scanned set grows one module per CION round;
# swept so far: mandate (20260811.132333), scribe + vault (20260811.133322), pond
# (20260811.133845), granary's OWN .rye prose (20260811.134946 — filenames kept: the
# tools/granary_lap*.rish witness handles stay as stable identifiers per Keaton's
# "prose-only" ruling), and scribble + linengrow prose (20260811.142447), then linengrow's two
# lap-ordinal PRINT strings (20260811.144935 — neth_sim_witness.rye and
# open_asks_escrow_delivery.rye, rebuilt and their witnesses re-run GREEN; the
# open-asks device-wire lab is a pre-existing qemu/virtio env limitation, not this
# change), then amphora prose (20260812.222457 — LOWE-J14r1, the first VOLS-surveyed
# prose gap relabeled to semantic label + stamp: manifest_entry.rye and
# vessel_fetch_delivery.rye headers named by capability, README's lap-1/2/3 shorthand
# reworded to point at the kept amphora_lap1/2/3.rish witness handles), then the comlink
# device-guest prose (20260812.223000 — LOWE-J14r2: the sixteen guest_*_tx/rx.rye that
# carried a BARE lap ordinal beside a structured code (OA-L3 lap 2, I2 snapshot lap 3,
# NS-L3 wire lap 2, Amphora lap 3) relabeled to structured-code + device role + stamp,
# and comlink/README.md's three bare-ordinal port-table labels named by device; the
# guest binaries are unchanged (a doc-comment header is never printed, so the
# qemu/virtio device-wire witnesses are untouched — only prose moved), then the three
# Q-vane voice modules (20260812.224144 — LOWE-J14r3: lattice · ember · lantern READMEs
# and authored .rye/.rish prose relabeled to semantic label + stamp — a version ordinal
# like "(lap 39)" or "Lantern lap 33 selftest" dropped for the capability's name + its
# git-author stamp, and lantern/README.md's 29-row fixtures table stripped of its "Lap N"
# provenance prefix, each fixture kept by its own purpose; the voice binaries build and
# pass GREEN through buhr_inference_query / buhr_reading_query / gism_j5_corpus_real_ember,
# a comment-only change), then the market + accounting modules (20260812.224144 —
# LOWE-J14r4a: mandi + dimeroll READMEs and authored .rye prose relabeled — Mandi's
# lap-1/lap-3 version headers named by capability (market listing · listing settle) and
# its README section headings named by feature, dimeroll's lap-2/lap-4 feature comments
# and its README status/design/link labels named by report (the dimeroll_sight_view_lap3.rish
# tool handle kept, and the dated design-doc filenames left untouched); mandi + dimeroll
# build GREEN through mandi_listing_settle / mandi_lap1 / dimeroll_lap4 / gism_ayre_j8),
# then the Nock interop (20260812.224721 — LOWE-J14r4b: glow/nock's phased-plan prose named
# by phase — "Lap 1 — the primitive core" → "The primitive core", "Lap 2 — the macro layer"
# → "The macro layer", "Lap 3 — the edit primitive" → "The edit primitive" — across
# nock_core.rye, nock_core_witness.rye (its GREEN print string relabeled off "lap 1", the
# witness asserting on GREEN/autocons not the ordinal), and README.md; the nock_lap2_witness.rye
# handle kept in a reworded reference; nock_core_witness GREEN), then the mantra weave
# (20260812.225213 — LOWE-J14r4c: mantra's snapshot/recall prose named by capability —
# "NS-L3 wire lap 1" → "NS-L3 wire", "I2 snapshot export lap 3" → "I2 snapshot export",
# "Lap 1 reuses"/"Lap 2 adds" → "Snapshot frames reuse"/"Horizon bundles add" — across
# README.md and the four snapshot/recall .rye (their hosted GREEN print strings relabeled
# off the ordinal; no witness asserts contains on them, only .ok, verified). The hosted
# witnesses mantra_snapshot_replay/horizon build snapshot_export.rye GREEN; the recall_sync
# device-wire lab is a pre-existing qemu/virtio env limit (git-stash A/B: baseline fails
# identically), not this change).
# Still deferred:
# the witness-asserted "SLC-2a Lap" scheme
# (linengrow/wayland_seed.rye + pond/slc2a witnesses) and comlink's sub-lap — a
# coupled cross-cutting round of its own. Dated
# session logs and specs keep the ordinals they recorded (testimony is never
# rewritten). Law addendum 20260811.130827:
# context/specs/20260810-222755_chronological-semantic-labeling-and-the-cion-meta-season.md

say "cion-module: Language EN — the labeling law, widened past the three pins to modules."
say "cion-module: Style Radiant — a capability's name is its semantic label + stamp, never a bare lap ordinal."
say "cion-module: Lens TAME — guard the living module surfaces; a planted lap ordinal must bite."

# The swept modules name no capability by a bare lap ordinal.
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/labeling_module_scan.sh" "mandate/README.md" "mandate/store.rye" "mandate/keyed.rye" "mandate/bucket.rye" "mandate/wal.rye" "mandate/serve.rye" "mandate/named_serve.rye" "mandate/comlink_serve.rye" "scribe/README.md" "scribe/reader.rye" "vault/README.md" "vault/shard.rye" "pond/README.md" "pond/apps/drawn_terminal.rye" "granary/README.md" "granary/exchange_listing.rye" "granary/resin_serve_delivery.rye" "granary/weave_settle.rye" "granary/weave_settle_core.rye" "scribble/README.md" "scribble/scribble.rye" "scribble/scribble_core.rye" "linengrow/README.md" "linengrow/wov_core.rye" "linengrow/neth_sim.rye" "linengrow/disclosure_core.rye" "linengrow/wov_tb_host.rye" "linengrow/neth_sim_witness.rye" "linengrow/open_asks_escrow_delivery.rye" "amphora/README.md" "amphora/manifest_entry.rye" "amphora/vessel_fetch_delivery.rye" "comlink/README.md" "comlink/guest_open_asks_escrow_hold_rx.rye" "comlink/guest_open_asks_escrow_hold_tx.rye" "comlink/guest_open_asks_escrow_release_rx.rye" "comlink/guest_open_asks_escrow_release_tx.rye" "comlink/guest_snapshot_fetcher_rx.rye" "comlink/guest_snapshot_fetcher_tx.rye" "comlink/guest_snapshot_source_rx.rye" "comlink/guest_snapshot_source_tx.rye" "comlink/guest_sync_fetcher_rx.rye" "comlink/guest_sync_fetcher_tx.rye" "comlink/guest_sync_source_rx.rye" "comlink/guest_sync_source_tx.rye" "comlink/guest_vessel_fetch_fetcher_rx.rye" "comlink/guest_vessel_fetch_fetcher_tx.rye" "comlink/guest_vessel_fetch_source_rx.rye" "comlink/guest_vessel_fetch_source_tx.rye" "lattice/README.md" "lattice/lattice_core.rye" "lattice/lattice.rye" "ember/README.md" "ember/ember_core.rye" "lantern/README.md" "lantern/lantern_core.rye" "lantern/lantern.rye" "mandi/README.md" "mandi/mandi_core.rye" "mandi/mandi.rye" "mandi/listing_settle_core.rye" "mandi/listing_settle.rye" "dimeroll/README.md" "dimeroll/dimeroll_core.rye" "dimeroll/dimeroll.rye" "glow/nock/README.md" "glow/nock/nock_core.rye" "glow/nock/nock_core_witness.rye" "mantra/README.md" "mantra/recall_sync_delivery.rye" "mantra/recall_sync_wire.rye" "mantra/snapshot_export_delivery.rye" "mantra/snapshot_export.rye"]
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "cion-module: a swept-module surface names a capability by a bare lap ordinal"
# values_apart: the verdict key and the exit status must agree.
assert scan.ok else "cion-module: mandate verdict and status disagree"

# The guard bites — a planted bare lap ordinal is caught on every run.
let neg = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/labeling_module_scan.sh" "tools/fixtures/labeling_module_negative.md"]
say neg.out
assert neg.out contains "verdict=drift" else "cion-module: planted lap ordinal was not flagged"
assert (neg.ok == false) else "cion-module: the guard failed to bite the planted negative"

# The guard stays quiet on the meaningful schemes the law permits — a structured code
# (lap 3w-3b, lap 4b, OA-L3, NS-L3) and a sub-lap compound must NOT trip it. A blocking
# guard earns a known-good fixture beside its known-bad one (refined 20260811.140623).
let pass = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/labeling_module_scan.sh" "tools/fixtures/labeling_module_pass.md"]
say pass.out
assert pass.out contains "verdict=ok" else "cion-module: the guard false-positived on a meaningful code or sub-lap"
assert pass.ok else "cion-module: pass-fixture verdict and status disagree"

say "GREEN: cion-module — the swept modules (mandate · scribe · vault · pond · granary · scribble · linengrow · amphora · comlink device guests · lattice · ember · lantern · mandi · dimeroll · glow/nock · mantra) name every capability by semantic label + stamp, no bare lap ordinal; the guard bites a planted one and stays quiet on meaningful codes"
